              "sectionSpacing": 8,
              "source": "\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:14.5px;color:#C9D2E0;line-height:1.55;padding:0 0 16px 0;\"\u003eSettle the shift for this die. You still read the press counter \u0026ndash; the system works out what each cavity is owed \u0026ndash; but now you also confirm what actually landed in each basket, cavity by cavity, and nothing is hidden just because a cavity has no basket at all.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e1\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eRead the line above the boxes\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eIt tells you where this die already stands for the shift \u0026ndash; \"This die is at 1,850 for the shift (recorded 14:22 by RMB)\", or \"Nothing recorded for this die yet this shift. Every cavity is credited from 0.\"\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:12.5px;color:#9AA8BF;font-style:italic;padding:2px 0 14px 46px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eIf it says \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eset by hand\u003c/span\u003e, someone has already corrected the counter this shift, and the reason is on the end of the line.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e2\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003ePick the shift\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eChoose your \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eShift\u003c/span\u003e.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e3\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eRead the press counter\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eType the number showing on the press counter right now into \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003ePress counter reading now\u003c/span\u003e. It is the counter\u0027s own reading, not a count of shots since your last entry.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:12.5px;color:#9AA8BF;font-style:italic;padding:2px 0 14px 46px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eNormally the counter starts from zero each shift and only ever climbs. If it was zeroed mid-shift, or someone typed a wrong number earlier, do not try to work around it \u0026ndash; use the button below.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#3A2E10;border-left:5px solid #F4B343;border-radius:4px;padding:12px 14px;margin:4px 0 16px 0;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;padding-bottom:4px;\"\u003eIf the counter was reset, or a wrong number went in earlier\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;line-height:1.5;\"\u003ePress \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eCounter reset / wrong total?\u003c/span\u003e. Enter what the counter actually reads now \u0026ndash; \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eif it was zeroed, enter 0\u003c/span\u003e \u0026ndash; pick why it moved, and confirm. Crediting resumes from that number. Pieces already on the baskets are NOT changed, and the die keeps the shot count it already has.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e4\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eCheck the die-wide block\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eBefore you look at any cavity, check \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eDie-wide\u003c/span\u003e on the right. It carries two named rows every shift \u0026ndash; \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eWarm-up shots\u003c/span\u003e (\u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eDC-999\u003c/span\u003e) and \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eQuality test shots\u003c/span\u003e (\u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003e107\u003c/span\u003e) \u0026ndash; plus \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003e+ Add die-wide scrap\u003c/span\u003e for anything else that happens to the whole die at once. Enter each one in \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eshots\u003c/span\u003e the press actually made, not a piece total \u0026ndash; the screen states the part count next to it, so nobody has to multiply by the number of cavities in their head.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:12.5px;color:#9AA8BF;font-style:italic;padding:2px 0 14px 46px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eThese shots come out of every cavity\u0027s count before anything else is worked out. A shift with 20 warm-up shots no longer shows up as 20 pieces of unexplained variance on every cavity \u0026ndash; it is accounted for here, once, for the whole die.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e5\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eCheck the Good figure on each cavity\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eIt starts out following the press counter on its own \u0026ndash; shots owed, minus that cavity\u0027s own scrap. The moment you type a number yourself it locks to that and is marked so you can see it was entered by hand. A line that just reads the counter types nothing here; a line that counts baskets types one number per cavity. There is no setting to choose \u0026ndash; it works either way, row by row.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:12.5px;color:#9AA8BF;font-style:italic;padding:2px 0 14px 46px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eA cavity with no basket has no \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eGood\u003c/span\u003e box to type into \u0026ndash; there is nowhere for those pieces to be counted yet. See step 7.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e6\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eLog any cavity scrap\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eTap the number under \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eCavity scrap\u003c/span\u003e on that cavity\u0027s row to add a reason and a quantity. It opens right where you tapped \u0026ndash; there is no separate screen \u0026ndash; and the chip beside the number shows how many reasons are already logged.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e7\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eA cavity with no basket\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eA cavity marked \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003ePending\u003c/span\u003e is not a problem. Its row reads something like \"116 shots since 02:10 \u0026ndash; credits to the next basket.\" Those shots are not lost: the moment a basket is opened in that cavity, it is credited everything run since, because that is physically where the castings are. A \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003ePending\u003c/span\u003e cavity never holds up Submit, and you can still log scrap against it if you know some of what it ran was bad.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e8\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eIf a Variance turns amber, say why\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eTap the number to pick a reason: the basket count was wrong, the press counter reading looked suspect, scrap happened but was not recorded, or parts were pulled off the line. Two of those ask for a short note as well.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#093240;border-left:5px solid #22A8CC;border-radius:4px;padding:12px 14px;margin:4px 0 16px 0;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:14px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;padding-bottom:4px;\"\u003eWhen you genuinely do not know, say that\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;line-height:1.5;\"\u003e\u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eUnknown\u003c/span\u003e is always on the list, and choosing it is the right, professional answer when you cannot account for the difference \u0026ndash; it is not a shortcut past the question. A screen that refuses to submit at 03:00 is what pushes an operator into picking a defect code at random, and that guess becomes a real reject on the report Honda reads. Add the short note it asks for \u0026ndash; a line like \u0026ldquo;found the cavity empty at 02:40\u0026rdquo; is worth more six months from now than a bare code.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"46\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:17px;background-color:#22A8CC;color:#0B1220;font-size:17px;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;line-height:34px;\"\u003e9\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-top:2px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eSubmit\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;padding-top:3px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003ePress \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eSubmit shift entry\u003c/span\u003e. It writes everything on this tab in one go \u0026ndash; every cavity\u0027s good count and scrap, and the die-wide block together.\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:12.5px;color:#9AA8BF;font-style:italic;padding:2px 0 14px 46px;line-height:1.5;\"\u003eWhile any cavity has a variance with no reason, the button stays disabled and the line beside it says how many \u0026ndash; \u0026ldquo;2 cavities need a reason\u0026rdquo; \u0026ndash; never that the numbers have to match. Fixing that is picking a reason, not forcing the count to balance.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"border-top:1px solid #172238;margin:2px 0 16px 0;\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"background-color:#172238;border-radius:6px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 12px 0;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style\u003d\"font-size:12px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.03em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#9AA8BF;padding-bottom:8px;\"\u003eTHE TOTALS ROW\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable width\u003d\"100%\" cellpadding\u003d\"0\" cellspacing\u003d\"0\" border\u003d\"0\" style\u003d\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"18\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;color:#22A8CC;font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;padding-bottom:10px;\"\u003e\u0026bull;\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-bottom:10px;\"\u003e\u003cspan style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eThe equation\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;line-height:1.5;\"\u003e \u0026ndash; Reads \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eShots minus Good minus Scrap equals Unaccounted\u003c/span\u003e across the bottom, in that order. Only cavities with a basket count toward \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003eUnaccounted\u003c/span\u003e \u0026ndash; a \u003cspan style\u003d\"color:#F0F3F8;font-weight:bold;\"\u003ePending\u003c/span\u003e cavity\u0027s shots show in their own figure, not folded into it.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr style\u003d\"border:none;\"\u003e\u003ctd width\u003d\"18\" valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;color:#22A8CC;font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;padding-bottom:10px;\"\u003e\u0026bull;\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd valign\u003d\"top\" style\u003d\"border:none;background-color:#172238;padding-bottom:10px;\"\u003e\u003cspan style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;font-weight:bold;color:#F0F3F8;\"\u003eDie life\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan style\u003d\"font-size:13.5px;color:#C9D2E0;line-height:1.5;\"\u003e \u0026ndash; The shots-vs-limit figure that used to sit in a right-hand panel is a pill in the header now. It turns amber as the die nears its shot limit \u0026ndash; look there instead of a sidebar.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e",
              "style": {
                "fontSize": 13,
                "overflow": "auto"
              }
            },
